{
  "_comment": [
    "M7.1 fixture: two default routes, over Ethernet and over Wi-Fi.",
    "",
    "This is what a laptop with both a wired and a wireless uplink looks like.",
    "Both links are real hardware, both are connected, both carry a default",
    "route, and both addresses are RFC1918.",
    "",
    "Two things are being defended here. First, this is a FACT and not a FAULT:",
    "an analysis that reported it as a broken configuration would be teaching",
    "the operator to ignore everything else the report says. Second, both",
    "current-route relationships must be visible — neither default route is",
    "more real than the other, and picking one of them would be picking for the",
    "operator.",
    "",
    "Addresses are chosen to defeat the other two shortcuts as well: the wired",
    "side carries 10.x and the wireless side carries 192.168.x, so classifying",
    "by address range would get both wrong."
  ],
  "links": [
    {
      "ifindex": 1,
      "ifname": "lo",
      "flags": ["LOOPBACK", "UP", "LOWER_UP"],
      "mtu": 65536,
      "operstate": "UNKNOWN",
      "link_type": "loopback",
      "address": "00:00:00:00:00:00",
      "broadcast": "00:00:00:00:00:00",
      "linkinfo": { "info_kind": "loopback" }
    },
    {
      "ifindex": 2,
